<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  VirtualDriver verification scenario 06_route_lane / lane_change_to_exit_ramp_at_constant_speed

  vd-func:FUNC-061 (indicator pre-signal before lane-change initiation) /
  req-vd-ad:REQ-AD-018 (法定タイミング要求 - JP Road Traffic Act Enforcement
  Order Art. 21 para 1: signal at least 3 seconds before the maneuver). This
  scenario isolates ladder step b ("定速で法定3秒のリードを満たす") from the
  two existing lane_change_to_exit_ramp*.xosc scenarios in this directory,
  neither of which can show a clean steady-state lead: both start Ego in a
  lane requiring n_remaining=3 hops (-1 or -2 to reach -4), for which
  required_m = 3*max(v*lane_change_lead_time_s, lane_change_min_lead_distance_m)
  + lane_change_reserve_distance_m = 3*(13.889*6.0)+20 = 270 m exceeds the
  190 m of road-0 travel available (road 0 is 200 m long, Ego starts at
  s=10) - so the first lane change is already decided on frame 1, before
  any lead measurement is possible (see the sibling files' header comments).

  This scenario instead starts Ego in lane -3 (not -1/-2), one hop from the
  target band: junction 1 connection id=3's <laneLink> covers ONLY "-4" of
  road 0 (measured fact, see lane_change_initiation.md section 3), so lane
  -3 needs exactly ONE lane change, -3 -> -4, i.e. n_remaining=1. At
  EgoSpeed=9.0 m/s (see the "WHY EgoSpeed IS 9.0 m/s" paragraph below for
  why this scenario does NOT use the sibling scenarios' 13.889 m/s),
  required_m = 1*max(9.0*6.0, 40)+20 = 74 m, comfortably inside the 190 m
  budget, so the hop arms partway through road 0 instead of at t=0 - the
  pre-signal and the arm both happen mid-run, where they can actually be
  measured apart.

  Route/road facts otherwise match the sibling scenarios exactly: same xodr
  (highway_example_with_merge_and_split.xodr), same junction 1 / connecting
  road 4, same explicit road-4 Waypoint (REQUIRED for Route::IsValid()==true
  - dropping it reproduces merge_required_for_exit_ramp.xosc's
  invalid_route case instead; see lane_change_to_exit_ramp.xosc's header
  comment for the full Route::IsValid()/RoadPath::Calculate explanation).

  CONSTANT SPEED, NOT A STORY RAMP: Ego's speed is set ONCE, in Init, via a
  step (instantaneous) SpeedAction - the same PrivateAction pattern this
  directory's lane_change_to_exit_ramp_with_traffic.xosc uses for its
  AdjacentTraffic entity - placed BEFORE the ControllerAction so the engine
  applies it while it still owns the LONG domain (see
  ControllerVirtualDriver.cpp's ResolveTargetSpeed: once no Story SpeedAction
  is ever observed running, the resolved target speed snaps to and stays at
  the last action's target forever). No Story Event touches Ego's speed at
  all (see Story/Act below: an empty ManeuverGroup, the same shape
  01_vehicle_model/straight_constant_speed.xosc uses). This deliberately
  avoids the sibling scenarios' 3.0s linear acceleration ramp, which is
  exactly the transient step c (req-vd-ad:REQ-AD-017) needs to be measured
  separately from (see lane_change_to_exit_ramp.expectations.yaml's must #3
  reason: for how that ramp compresses the measured lead to 0.40s).

  WHY EgoSpeed IS 9.0 m/s, NOT 13.889 m/s (2026-08-03, parent session, real
  post-fix Release build with the forward-projection indicator rule
  (section 11-11) wired in): the value of the speed itself carries no
  meaning for this scenario - what matters is pushing the decision instant
  (t_arm) out past the point where the driver model's speed-tracking
  transient has actually settled. At 13.889 m/s the -3 -> -4 hop decides at
  t_sig~=3.25 / t_arm~=6.20, which sits in the MIDDLE of that transient:
  measured d(ego.speed)/dt at those times was still +0.0241 m/s^2 at t=3.0,
  +0.0079 m/s^2 at t=6.0, only reaching +0.0009 m/s^2 at t=10.0 and
  +0.00003 m/s^2 at t=15.0. Deciding mid-transient is why 13.889 m/s
  measured a lead of 2.95s instead of the clean 3.00s this scenario exists
  to demonstrate - not quantization, not a rule defect. Lowering EgoSpeed to
  9.0 m/s pushes both thresholds later (t_sig~=9.9s, t_arm~=12.9s, both
  past t=10s where a<0.001 m/s^2), so the hop is decided against a speed
  that has already converged, i.e. genuinely constant for the purposes of
  the two-threshold rule.

  EXPECTED (arithmetic, confirmed by measurement - see this file's
  expectations.yaml) at EgoSpeed=9.0 m/s: n_remaining=1, lane_change_lead_
  time_s=6.0, lane_change_min_lead_distance_m=40, lane_change_reserve_
  distance_m=20, lane_change_indicator_lead_time_s=3.0, dist_to_connection
  at the s=10 teleport = 190 m (road 0 is 200 m long):
    required_m = 1 * max(9.0*6.0, 40) + 20 = 54 + 20 = 74 m
    signal threshold = required_m + v*3.0 = 74 + 27 = 101 m
      -> t_sig = (190-101)/9.0 = 9.9 s
    arm threshold    = required_m = 74 m
      -> t_arm = (190-74)/9.0 = 12.9 s
    lead = t_arm - t_sig = 3.0 s exactly (3v/v = 3.0s, the same "closing
    rate is exactly v" degeneracy as before, now measured with a converged
    speed instead of a mid-transient one) - see the with-traffic sibling's
    expectations.yaml notes for the same derivation shape.
-->
<OpenSCENARIO>
   <FileHeader revMajor="1"
               revMinor="1"
               date="2026-08-03T10:00:00"
               description="VirtualDriver verification: AD-initiated lane change to reach a junction exit ramp at constant speed, isolating the steady-state 3.0s indicator lead"
               author="GT_esmini"/>
   <ParameterDeclarations>
      <ParameterDeclaration name="EgoSpeed" parameterType="double" value="9.0"/>
   </ParameterDeclarations>
   <CatalogLocations/>
   <RoadNetwork>
      <LogicFile filepath="../../../xodr/highway_example_with_merge_and_split.xodr"/>
   </RoadNetwork>
   <Entities>
      <ScenarioObject name="Ego">
         <Vehicle name="car_white" vehicleCategory="car" model3d="../../../models/car_white.osgb">
            <BoundingBox>
               <Center x="1.4" y="0.0" z="0.9"/>
               <Dimensions width="2.0" length="5.0" height="1.8"/>
            </BoundingBox>
            <Performance maxSpeed="69" maxDeceleration="30" maxAcceleration="10"/>
            <Axles>
               <FrontAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="2.98" positionZ="0.4"/>
               <RearAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="0" positionZ="0.4"/>
            </Axles>
            <Properties>
               <Property name="model_id" value="0"/>
               <Property name="scaleMode" value="ModelToBB"/>
            </Properties>
         </Vehicle>
         <ObjectController>
            <Controller name="VirtualDriverController">
               <Properties>
                  <Property name="esminiController" value="VirtualDriverController"/>
               </Properties>
            </Controller>
         </ObjectController>
      </ScenarioObject>
   </Entities>
   <Storyboard>
      <Init>
         <Actions>
            <Private entityRef="Ego">
               <PrivateAction>
                  <TeleportAction>
                     <Position>
                        <LanePosition roadId="0" laneId="-3" offset="0" s="10"/>
                     </Position>
                  </TeleportAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <!--
                 Constant speed, set ONCE here (step / 0.0s time), BEFORE the
                 ControllerAction below hands the LONG domain to
                 VirtualDriverController - see the file-level header comment
                 for why the ordering matters. No Story Event ever touches
                 Ego's speed (see the empty ManeuverGroup below), so this is
                 the only speed command Ego ever receives.
               -->
               <PrivateAction>
                  <LongitudinalAction>
                     <SpeedAction>
                        <SpeedActionDynamics dynamicsShape="step" value="0.0" dynamicsDimension="time"/>
                        <SpeedActionTarget>
                           <AbsoluteTargetSpeed value="$EgoSpeed"/>
                        </SpeedActionTarget>
                     </SpeedAction>
                  </LongitudinalAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <RoutingAction>
                     <AssignRouteAction>
                        <Route name="ego_route" closed="false">
                           <!--
                             Start Waypoint matches the TeleportAction above: lane -3,
                             one hop from the target band {-4} (junction 1 connection
                             id=3 covers only "-4" of road 0 - see the file-level
                             header comment). n_remaining=1, unlike the -1/-2 starts
                             of the sibling scenarios in this directory.
                           -->
                           <Waypoint routeStrategy="shortest">
                              <Position>
                                 <LanePosition roadId="0" laneId="-3" offset="0" s="10"/>
                              </Position>
                           </Waypoint>
                           <!--
                             Explicit connecting-road Waypoint (junction 1, connection
                             id=3) - required for Route::IsValid()==true. See
                             lane_change_to_exit_ramp.xosc's header comment.
                           -->
                           <Waypoint routeStrategy="shortest">
                              <Position>
                                 <LanePosition roadId="4" laneId="-1" offset="0" s="50"/>
                              </Position>
                           </Waypoint>
                           <Waypoint routeStrategy="shortest">
                              <Position>
                                 <LanePosition roadId="2" laneId="-1" offset="0" s="40"/>
                              </Position>
                           </Waypoint>
                        </Route>
                     </AssignRouteAction>
                  </RoutingAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <ControllerAction>
                     <ActivateControllerAction lateral="true" longitudinal="true"/>
                  </ControllerAction>
               </PrivateAction>
            </Private>
         </Actions>
      </Init>
      <!--
        Deliberately empty ManeuverGroup - same shape as
        01_vehicle_model/straight_constant_speed.xosc. No Maneuver/Event
        means no Story-level action ever runs against Ego's speed, so
        ControllerVirtualDriver::ResolveTargetSpeed never observes a RUNNING
        LONG_SPEED action after Init and snaps to (and stays at) the Init
        step action's target for the whole run - i.e. truly constant speed,
        not merely "no additional ramp on top of one". See the file-level
        header comment.
      -->
      <Story name="RouteLaneStory">
         <Act name="RouteLaneAct">
            <ManeuverGroup maximumExecutionCount="1" name="EgoGroup">
               <Actors selectTriggeringEntities="false">
                  <EntityRef entityRef="Ego"/>
               </Actors>
            </ManeuverGroup>
            <StartTrigger>
               <ConditionGroup>
                  <Condition name="ActStart" delay="0" conditionEdge="none">
                     <ByValueCondition>
                        <SimulationTimeCondition value="0" rule="greaterThan"/>
                     </ByValueCondition>
                  </Condition>
               </ConditionGroup>
            </StartTrigger>
         </Act>
      </Story>
      <StopTrigger>
         <ConditionGroup>
            <Condition name="StopCondition" delay="0" conditionEdge="rising">
               <ByValueCondition>
                  <SimulationTimeCondition value="28" rule="greaterThan"/>
               </ByValueCondition>
            </Condition>
         </ConditionGroup>
      </StopTrigger>
   </Storyboard>
</OpenSCENARIO>
